I'm currently rewriting the save system to avoid these sorts of
problems. First time I've seen one on a local game, though, which gives
me some interesting insight into the bug (it can't be server-specific).
Also, the message about notifying daniel_t is left in there unchanged
from NitroHack in 4.1.2 (I've been modifying it more recently). This
message is amusing in context (NitroHack's save system is incredibly
buggy).

However, the good thing about this is that this sort of save corruption
is usually recoverable, although it can take a lot of effort to do so.
Make a backup of the save file first, just in case something goes wrong.
My advice is to delete everything after byte 966477 in the file, then
to continue deleting backwards from the end until that the last line
of the file starts with '~' and ends with a newline. Finally, there
are two numbers in the header (written as 8 digits each, in
hexadecimal): you need to change the larger to equal the new length of
the file in bytes.

This recovery method doesn't always work; its success rate is maybe
about 50%. If it doesn't work, let me know
and I'll see if I can recover it myself. (Note that whether it fails
or succeeds, the file will be marked as "crashed" in the menu; just
try to load it anyway.)

If the recovery does work, then after getting back into the game, play
one turn, save, and reload; this minimizes the chance of residual
problems caused by the recovery.

